{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And the sons of Aaron the priests shall put fire.</b> Even though fire descends from heaven, it is a commandment to bring [fire] from an ordinary source, in order to mingle the fire from above with the fire from below, and to judge the sinner in two courts — to atone for the contemplation of the kind of sin that was liable to be judged in the court above, and for the contemplation of the kind of sin that was liable to be judged in the court below. And this is the meaning of ״סַמְּכוּנִי בָאֲשִׁישׁוֹת״ (Song of Songs 2:5) — two kinds of fire, ״כִּי חוֹלַת אַהֲבָה אָנִי״ — these are the sins, the illness of the soul that afflicts one in love of HaShem, blessed be He, and he is healed through these two fires."], :book :leviticus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Reading הֶעָוֹן in the first clause and הַחֵטְא in the second as distinguishing between sins judged above (עָוֹן) and below (חֵטְא); the word מִין ('kind') is preserved in both clauses."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:35:00.000938234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}